WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.150
This next story is sort of the perfect epitome
of everything that is Donald Trump.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:11.520
According to the former Department of Homeland
Security chief of staff, Miles Taylor, Donald

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:18.590
Trump floated the idea of swapping Puerto
Rico for Greenland in order to get rid of

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:23.840
some of those poor Puerto Ricans from dirty
Puerto Rico.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.410
Yeah, this Kombai is like three or four different
stories.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:33.420
So first, of course, is Trump's obvious disregard
for Puerto Rico.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.070
We saw this during hurricane response in the
past.

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:40.880
You might remember Donald Trump showing up
in Puerto Rico and shooting rolls of paper

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.329
towels like basketballs.

00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:49.170
Then there's the idea of the asshole country,
which mostly are countries with brown people.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:53.060
And then there's the idea of Trump being interested
in acquiring Greenland, which is something

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:54.060
that came up.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.239
I don't know if it was six months ago or twelve
months ago.

00:00:56.239 --> 00:00:58.750
Just time feels so strange at this point.

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:05.959
And lastly, kind of tying it all together
is Donald Trump's completely deranged worldview,

00:01:05.959 --> 00:01:10.500
his delusions of grandeur, his narcissism,
his complete lack of empathy.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.630
So let's first go to the tape.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.799
Here is Myles Taylor, former Department of
Homeland Security chief of staff, telling

00:01:17.799 --> 00:01:21.499
the story himself on MSNBC, tear gas at the
border, etc..

00:01:21.499 --> 00:01:24.409
I wonder what is the most in the conversations
are involved in.

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:29.060
Disturbing idea or thought or discussion that
you heard from President Trump?

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:33.659
That is sort of resonating and sitting with
you and still today.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:37.060
We could probably go on for days about that,
although I'm going to tell you one thing that

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:40.100
just popped into my head, Howie.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:44.889
There was a time when, of course, we were
spending a lot of our days down in Puerto

00:01:44.889 --> 00:01:50.359
Rico after the hurricanes wreaked devastation
down there, U.S. Virgin Islands and other

00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:54.279
places where there was a trip that we made
down there in August of 2018.

00:01:54.279 --> 00:01:58.659
And I remember before we went, the president
said something.

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:00.939
And your viewers are going to be somewhat
familiar with this.

00:02:00.939 --> 00:02:04.659
The president's talked before about wanting
to purchase Greenland.

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:08.810
But one time before we went down, he told
us not only did he want to purchase Greenland,

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:12.090
he actually said he wanted to see if we could
sell Puerto Rico.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.670
Could we swap where do Rico for Greenland?

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:19.230
Because in his words, Puerto Rico was dirty
and the people were poor.

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:23.780
These are Americans, Halli, and we don't talk
about our fellow Americans that way.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:29.739
So this is really pretty wild and completely
unconscionable and really something to contend

00:02:29.739 --> 00:02:30.739
with.

00:02:30.739 --> 00:02:34.659
It has to be an anecdote for some kind of
Hall of fame, although I don't know what we

00:02:34.659 --> 00:02:37.850
would be commemorating in this Hall of Fame,
it wouldn't be anything good.

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:41.430
But it seems like that anecdote is historic
in some sense.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:47.379
And I'm reminded of what Michelle Obama told
us during her DNC speech on the first night

00:02:47.379 --> 00:02:52.480
of the Democratic National Convention Monday,
which was, if you think things couldn't possibly

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.769
get any worse, they can and they will if we
don't make a change this election now merely

00:02:57.769 --> 00:03:00.230
as a thought experiment.

00:03:00.230 --> 00:03:06.620
If Puerto Rico got to become part of Denmark,
the way Greenland is part of Denmark now,

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:11.849
Puerto Ricans might actually be better off
because my guess is Denmark wouldn't do to

00:03:11.849 --> 00:03:18.400
Puerto Rico or neglect Puerto Rico in the
way that Donald Trump has neglected Puerto

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.400
Rico.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:24.469
So from the standpoint of the Puerto Rican
people, it may be interesting to them to actually

00:03:24.469 --> 00:03:25.880
become part of Denmark.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:29.969
But of course, this is completely crazy in
every sense.

00:03:29.969 --> 00:03:34.439
And it's very funny to hear the right continue
to insist that Latino voters are just that

00:03:34.439 --> 00:03:35.579
they're on the verge.

00:03:35.579 --> 00:03:40.200
They're so close of becoming Republicans and
abandoning the Democratic Party.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:44.049
Then you hear this, and it's very hard to
fathom that that's the case.

00:03:44.049 --> 00:03:50.659
And of course, Cubans are the most conservative
Latino group in the United States other than

00:03:50.659 --> 00:03:52.019
Cubans.

00:03:52.019 --> 00:03:59.609
There is very little Republicanism among Latino
Vought voters, Puerto Ricans, Dominicans,

00:03:59.609 --> 00:04:02.680
Mexicans, Argentineans, so on and so forth.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:09.700
And then, by the way, everybody who talked
about we need a business person running the

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:11.659
country like a business.

00:04:11.659 --> 00:04:13.249
This is what you get.

00:04:13.249 --> 00:04:18.199
This is what you get when you have someone
who says, if a piece of my business isn't

00:04:18.199 --> 00:04:24.680
interesting, if a piece piece of my business
is a loss leader, if it's not profitable or

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:25.720
